{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2193-07-10 20:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hello Mr. Johnson, I'm Dr. Patel, one of the surgical team members. You've been admitted because of a narrowing in the stent that was placed in the artery to your transplanted kidney. We saw this on your recent ultrasound."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2193-07-10 20:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, I remember that ultrasound. My blood pressure’s been going up again. Is that because of the stent?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2193-07-10 20:03:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, exactly. The ultrasound showed high blood flow speeds—433 and 464 cm/sec—which suggests the stent is narrowing again. That can reduce blood flow to your kidney and raise your blood pressure."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2193-07-10 20:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So what happens now? Another procedure?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2193-07-10 20:06:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. Tomorrow, you’ll have a procedure called angioplasty. We’ll go in through your groin, check the artery with imaging, and reopen the narrowed part of the stent."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2193-07-10 20:08:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I be asleep? Is it risky?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2193-07-10 20:09:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll be under light sedation—awake but relaxed. It’s generally safe. We’ll monitor your heart and oxygen closely. You’ve had a stent before, so we know your anatomy."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2193-07-10 20:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. And my kidney—will this help it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2193-07-10 20:12:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, restoring good blood flow should help your kidney function and control your blood pressure better. Your creatinine is 1.8 today—stable, which is good."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2193-07-10 20:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I’ve been taking all my meds—tacrolimus, Cellcept, the blood pressure pills. Should I keep them?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2193-07-10 20:15:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, keep taking them exactly as before. The transplant team checked—your tacrolimus level is stable. That’s important to avoid rejection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2193-07-10 20:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my diabetes? I’ve been checking my sugars."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2193-07-10 20:18:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your fingerstick was 178—reasonable. We’ll keep monitoring. You’ll stay on your insulin—Humalog and Lantus—as prescribed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2193-07-10 20:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. What about the chest X-ray they did earlier?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2193-07-10 20:21:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That was part of your pre-op check. It showed no heart or lung issues—clear lungs, normal heart size. So you’re cleared for the procedure."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2193-07-10 20:23:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good to hear. I was worried something else was wrong."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2193-07-10 20:24:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re being thorough. You also had labs—your electrolytes and kidney function are stable. We’ll give you extra fluids tonight to protect your kidney during tomorrow’s procedure."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2193-07-10 20:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "They mentioned something about a special dye?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2193-07-10 20:27:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll use CO2 gas instead of regular contrast dye. It’s safer for your kidney function. We also give bicarbonate and Mucomyst to help protect your kidneys."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2193-07-10 20:29:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That makes sense. I remember that from last time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2193-07-11 12:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi Mr. Johnson. You’re back from the procedure. Everything went very well. We confirmed the narrowing in the stent and reopened it with a balloon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2193-07-11 12:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No complications? How’s the kidney?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2193-07-11 12:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No issues. You stayed stable the whole time. Blood flow looks much better now. Your kidney should get the blood it needs."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2193-07-11 12:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my blood pressure?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2193-07-11 12:37:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll watch it closely. It may improve over the next few days. You’re still on your usual meds—amlodipine, lisinopril, metoprolol."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2193-07-11 12:39:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I feel okay—just a little sore at the groin."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2193-07-11 12:40:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s normal. We’ll keep an eye on the site for any bleeding. You need to keep your leg straight for a few hours to help it heal."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2193-07-11 12:42:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. Can I eat?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2193-07-11 12:43:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ll start with light food and advance as you tolerate. Drink plenty of fluids to help flush things out."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2193-07-11 15:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just checking in. Your vitals are stable—BP 158/72, pulse 64. The transplant team confirmed your tacrolimus level is still in range."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2193-07-11 15:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. Any infection risk?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2193-07-11 15:03:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your urine culture came back with low bacteria—less than 10,000—so no infection. You’re on Bactrim, which helps prevent urinary infections anyway."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2193-07-11 15:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Right, for the transplant. I’ve been on that for years."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2193-07-11 15:06:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. We’re not changing your immunosuppression. Everything’s staying the same unless needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2193-07-12 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your labs this morning show your creatinine is still 1.8—no change. That’s excellent after the procedure."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2193-07-12 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So I can go home today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2193-07-12 09:03:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, if you’re feeling well. We’ll send you home with instructions. You’ll stay on Plavix and aspirin to keep the stent open."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2193-07-12 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Same as before?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2193-07-12 09:06:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes—Plavix 75 mg daily, aspirin 81 mg. Continue all your other meds too. No heavy lifting for a week, and don’t drive while on pain meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2193-07-12 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And when do I follow up?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2193-07-12 09:09:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "See the vascular clinic in two weeks for a check-up and ultrasound. Call if you have fever, groin swelling, or leg pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2193-07-12 09:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. Thank you, doctor. I feel much better already."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2193-07-12 09:12:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Keep up with your healthy habits—good diet, meds on time, and monitor your blood pressure at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2193-07-12 09:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. And I’ll call if anything seems off."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2193-07-12 09:15:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. We’ll get your discharge papers ready. You’re doing great."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2193-07-10 19:42:00",
    "admission_end": "2193-07-12 13:00:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "Mr. Johnson, a male with a history of kidney transplant, type 2 diabetes, hypertension, and hyperlipidemia, was admitted for symptomatic in-stent restenosis of the renal artery to his transplanted kidney. He presented with elevated blood pressure, and a transplant kidney ultrasound revealed significantly increased renal artery velocities, confirming restenosis. He underwent elective angioplasty of the existing renal artery stent, which was performed successfully without complications. He remained hemodynamically stable throughout, with no change in kidney function post-procedure. His pain was controlled, and he tolerated a diet advance. He was discharged home in stable condition on day two with continued immunosuppressive, antihypertensive, and antiplatelet therapy, and instructions to follow up with vascular surgery in two weeks.",
    "problems": [
      "Other complications due to genitourinary device, implant, and graft",
      "Kidney replaced by transplant",
      "Diabetes mellitus without mention of complication, type II or unspecified type, not stated as uncontrolled",
      "Unspecified essential hypertension",
      "Pure hypercholesterolemia",
      "Atherosclerosis of renal artery",
      "Hyperplasia of prostate, unspecified, without urinary obstruction and other lower urinary symptoms (LUTS)",
      "Surgical operation with implant of artificial internal device causing abnormal patient reaction, or later complication,without mention of misadventure at time of operation",
      "Personal history of malignant neoplasm of other urinary organs",
      "Long-term (current) use of insulin"
    ]
  }
}
